@meta
id: 09-06
title: Put a count on the motion
chapter: 09
type: lesson
skills: op-counts, op-motion
par: 24
minutes: 4
vscode: drag-select three words, Delete, drag-select two more, type
open: policy.md

@brief
A policy note is being tightened before it goes to finance. Two edits:

    Finance want a hard and fast thirty day refund window.
    The window is thirty calendar days long.

The first line loses `hard and fast` — the sentence reads fine without
it. On the second line, `thirty calendar` becomes `30`, so it ends up as
`The window is 30 days long.`

@keys
| `d3w` | delete three words |
| `c2w` | change two words |
| `3w` | move three words — the same motion, without an operator |

@hints
A motion takes a count. That does not stop being true when there is an
operator in front of it.
--
`d3w` deletes the ground that `3w` would have covered. `c2w` changes the
ground `2w` covers and leaves you typing.
--
`3w` to reach `hard`, then `d3w`. Then `j0`, `3w` to reach `thirty`, then
`c2w` and type `30`.

@solution
    3w d3w    j 0 3w c2w 30 <Esc>    :wq<Enter>

The count sits with the motion because it belongs to the motion. `d3w` is
`d` applied to `3w`, in the same way `dw` is `d` applied to `w`. There is
no separate "delete three words" command to learn, and there is no list to
memorise — anything you can count as a movement, you can count as an edit.

Watch what `c2w` did on that second line. It ran from `thirty` over
`calendar` and stopped dead before `days`, leaving the space and the rest
of the sentence untouched. The `w` on the end of a count still lands where
`w` lands.

One warning that will save you a `u` later: the count is a number of
*motions*, not a number of things that look like words to a human. In code
a dot, a bracket and a comma are each a word. `d3w` on `order.total,` eats
`order`, `.` and `total` and stops. Counting words in prose is reliable.
Counting words in code is a coin toss, which is why the next few lessons
move on to motions that do not need counting at all.

@start policy.md
Finance want a hard and fast thirty day refund window.
The window is thirty calendar days long.

@expected policy.md
Finance want a thirty day refund window.
The window is 30 days long.
